source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:bba78d0db9c63799344439dc27ecc86b827daca50635d0fa22cbec07f915c9f0","file":"preprints/Sharp-binary-information-contraction-on-the-discrete-cube-September-24-2026/build/main.tex","line":72,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"6d26487c1ee6913ad22f80ec19daa221ee50555108ecd28b45bc092d14443e63","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Sharp-binary-information-contraction-on-the-discrete-cube-September-24-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:bba78d0db9c63799344439dc27ecc86b827daca50635d0fa22cbec07f915c9f0","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Sharp-binary-information-contraction-on-the-discrete-cube-September-24-2026/build/main.tex#L72"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{main:soft}\nFor every finite $n\\ge0$, every $u:\\Omega_n\\to[-1,1]$, and\n$-1\\le\\rho\\le1$,\n\\begin{equation}\n I(T_\\rho u)\n \\le\\psi\\!\\left(|\\rho|\\,\\psi^{-1}(I(u))\\right).\n \\label{main:interpolation}\n\\end{equation}\nThe inverse is the nonnegative increasing branch on $[0,L]$.\nFor $n\\ge1$, every soft coordinate $u(x)=a x_i$, $|a|\\le1$,\nattains equality."}
